{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sb7avzh624rydmjhmfircle6yxyv65bygkrcktll57uf2mwvlruq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases passed, and the Rust translation required **no fixes** — it is byte-identical to the C for every input I could construct.\n\n## What the target actually is\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` is `add_executable(driver src/main.c)` — a 25-line program, not a library. `nm -D --defined-only` on the C binary prints **nothing** (executables export no API symbols; its `.dynsym` holds only libc imports `printf`/`puts`/`strtol`). So the external boundary is the process contract, and the tests spawn *both real binaries* and compare stdout/stderr/exit status/terminating signal — never calling Rust in-process.\n\n## Phase A artifacts (crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | every `nm -D` symbol of the C binary, its Rust counterpart, entry points (`main`, `_start`) present in both, and a 66-symbol undefined audit → **0 missing non-libc symbols** |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 34 rows from the C's **two** rejection sites (`argc != 2`, `end == argv[1]`), plus the mirror table of inputs that *look* invalid but the C accepts (ERANGE clamp, int truncation, trailing garbage, UB overflow, write failures) |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 36 rows over the axes the C branches on (whitespace/sign/zeros/digit-count/magnitude class/last digit/sign-at-`%`/narrowing/`val++` overflow × stdout target × locale × env × argv0 × stdin) |\n\n## Results\n\n- **Phase B**: 37 tests, all 36 rows ✓ — randomized fixed-seed property tests (2048-case lexical cross-product, exhaustive `-300..=300`, exhaustive 255-byte sweep), plus **deep streaming comparison** (full 10M-line runs; first 256 MiB of the ~2^31-line `INT_MAX`-wrap runs).\n- **Phase C**: 32 tests, all 34 rows ✓ — including `argc == 0` via raw `execve` with `argv={NULL}`, closed fd 1, SIGPIPE parity, and one-step-past every bound.\n- **Phase D**: `[features] default = []` is the only feature set → all 69 tests pass under default/`--no-default-features` × debug/release (`./run_all.sh`), symbol diff empty, all imports resolve.\n\n## Confirmed quirks reproduced\n\nC's truncating `%` (so `-19 % 10 == -9` → never breaks early, counts to `+9`), `strtol` ERANGE clamp then `long`→`int` truncation (`LONG_MAX` → `-1`, `LONG_MIN` → `0`), signed-overflow wrap at `INT_MAX` → `INT_MIN`, partial parses, errors on **stdout**, and SIGPIPE/SIGXFSZ death parity.\n\n## Proof the tests have teeth\n\nSince everything passed first try, I added `mutation_check.py`: it injects 10 deliberate breakages into `src/main.rs` one at a time (rem_euclid, saturating narrowing, no SIGPIPE reset, checked overflow, message on stderr, rejecting trailing garbage, wrapping instead of clamping, altered message text, changed separator, rejecting `+`) and confirms the suite catches **all 10** — then restores and hash-verifies the source. `src/main.rs` is byte-identical to its pre-verification state, and nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1394,"cache_read_input_tokens":156597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1394,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c72e38d-7458-440b-9b2d-8f203be39e4b","uuid":"79760be0-7e0f-443d-b005-fb3c8521adb9","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:45:14.126Z"}
